    "jumpMps": 12.0,
    "trackingJumps": "A step between two consecutive frames faster than 12.0 m/s (more than 0.48 m in 0.04 s, faster than any footballer) is a tracking jump: a lost track freezes and then snaps to the real position. Every frame whose 0.4 s speed window contains a jump counts as minutes on the pitch but not in distance, high-speed distance, sprints (it ends a sprint run) or top speed.",
    "topSpeed": "Maximum smoothed (0.4 s) speed in metres per second, not the provider's instantaneous value.",
    "totals": "Per side, summed from unrounded player values and then rounded; topSpeed is the maximum of the side's players.",
    "sides": "home / away are the event fixture's labels: the lexicographically smaller club id is home, which is not necessarily the DFL home team."
